       Detailed Technical Specification

       1. Identity Resolution & Session Cookie Synchronization

       [0007]   Inbound HTTP requests pass through get_current_user(), which inspects reverse-proxy
       authentication headers (x-forwarded-user, x-claudia-user, x-tailscale-user), session cookies,
       and query parameters before defaulting to claudia_user. Legacy single-user records in SQLite are
       automatically migrated to the authenticated user profile upon login.

       [0008] At startup, ensure_cookies_file() verifies whether cookies.txt exists and is less than 24
       hours (86,400 seconds) old. When stale or missing, it extracts active session cookies from Firefox into a local
       Netscape cookie jar and pairs them with Node.js EJS runtime components and multi-client emulation (ios,
       web_embedded, android) to maintain reliable extraction.

       2. Search Pagination, Page Caching & Direct Stream Resolution

       [0009] The /api/search endpoint handles keyword queries, channel URLs (/@, /channel/, /c/, /
       user/), and playlist URLs across four content tabs (videos, shorts, live, playlists). Offset and limit
       parameters map directly to playliststart and playlistend for full collection paging, and serialized
       responses are cached in SQLite (page_cache).




ORIGINAL TECHNICAL SOURCE · PORTFOLIO APPENDIX                                                                APPENDIX / 4

       [0010] Playback requests hit /api/watch/{video_id} to record watch history and return metadata, while /
       api/media-stream/{video_id} resolves direct media stream URLs inside a thread-locked in-memory
       cache with a 15-minute Time-To-Live (TTL), falling back to an autoplay embed redirect if direct stream
       extraction is unavailable.

       3. Concurrent Download Manager & FFmpeg Postprocessing

       [0011] Batch download endpoints (/api/download/batch and /api/download/queue-batch) assign
       8-character UUID task identifiers and enqueue jobs into download_tasks with optional custom subdirectory
       routing under ~/localtube/downloads. A daemon worker loop (background_download_worker)
       polls every 0.5 seconds and enforces a configurable concurrency ceiling (defaulting to 2 simultaneous
       downloads).

       [0012] Each worker thread attaches a real-time progress_hook that computes completion percentage, transfer
       speed (MB/s), and estimated time remaining (ETA). Video jobs merge best video and audio streams into MP4
       containers, while audio jobs invoke FFmpegExtractAudio at 192 kbps (MP3, WAV, or M4A) before logging
       completed files into SQLite.

       4. Local Media Scanner, Creator Channels & AI Discovery

       [0013] The /api/media/library endpoint traverses configured local directories (~/Media/Videos/TV,
       ~/Media/Videos/Movies, ~/localtube/media, and ~/Videos) and applies regular-expression
       pattern matching ([sS](\d+)[eE](\d+)) to separate episodic television series by season and episode from
       standalone films.

       [0014] Additional modules enable local creator channels (user_channels and uploaded_videos),
       custom playlists with JSON export/import, playback resume tracking (progress_seconds), and an AI
       recommendation and chat assistant (/api/ai-suggestions and /api/ai-chat) that combines watch-
       history term scoring with 24-hour temporal dismissal cooldowns (temporal_dismissals) and upvote/
       downvote feedback.




