       Key Architectural Capabilities (Portfolio Summary)

        1. Unified Cloud-to-Local Media Bridge: Combines live video search, direct stream proxying, and local
             filesystem movie/TV indexing within a single self-hosted FastAPI service backed by SQLite.

        2. Resilient Multi-Client Extraction: Automates 24-hour Firefox cookie jar exports alongside Node.js EJS
             runtime execution and multi-client fallback profiles to prevent stream extraction failures.

        3. Controllable Multi-Threaded Download Queue: Supports batch queueing, custom destination folders,
             dynamic concurrency limits, individual or global pause/resume/stop controls, and real-time speed/ETA
             telemetry.

        4. Temporal Recommendation Suppression: Filters AI-generated video suggestions against a SQLite
             temporal_dismissals cooldown table so dismissed titles are suppressed for 24 hours rather than
             immediately resurfacing.

        5. Zero-Config Mesh Identity: Recognizes Tailscale and reverse-proxy identity headers out of the box to
             isolate watch history, subscriptions, playlists, and creator channels per household user.


       Abstract


          [0015] ClaudiaTube is a self-hosted media streaming, offline archival, and personal library platform built
          with Python, FastAPI, SQLite, yt-dlp, and FFmpeg. Engineered for local networks and Tailscale mesh
          deployments, the system integrates multi-tab video search, 15-minute TTL direct stream proxying, a multi-
          threaded batch download queue with live speed and ETA telemetry, regex-based local TV and movie library
          indexing, portable JSON playlists, and an AI-assisted discovery engine governed by 24-hour temporal
