       Core Subsystems & Features

       1. Electron Shell, Preload Bridge & Persistence

       [0006] The main process enables autoplay without user gesture requirements, creates a fullscreen frameless/auto-
       hidden-menu BrowserWindow loading renderer/index.html, intercepts the Escape key to close the
       window cleanly, and logs renderer errors and UI inspection snapshots after load. Channel definitions, media
       items, and settings are persisted to network.json in Electron's userData directory, while per-channel
       liveState and cached media durations are stored in live-state.json.

       [0007]      preload.js            uses    contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld('tv',                      ...)       with
       contextIsolation: true and nodeIntegration: false to expose typed IPC invoke/send/event
       methods and safe file URL conversion.

       2. Media Ingestion & Stream Resolution

       [0008] Users can import local directories (including role-specific folders) and multi-selected video/audio files via
       native open dialogs, or import online media from YouTube (via a local LocalTube endpoint such as
       http://127.0.0.1:8000, including channels, playlists, playlist collections, and individual videos),
       Dailymotion (via yt-dlp flat playlist metadata extraction), Archive.org items or direct /download/ video
       links, and direct HTML pages scanned for video links (with optional recursive folder traversal).




ORIGINAL TECHNICAL SOURCE · PORTFOLIO APPENDIX                                                                     APPENDIX / 4

       [0009] On playback or analysis, online:resolve-stream resolves yt-dlp stream URLs on demand or
       returns direct/LocalTube stream URLs, while media response headers on HTTP media requests are augmented
       when initiated from the app's file context.

       3. FFmpeg Black-Frame & Loudness Analysis

       [0010]     Two FFmpeg-backed analysis pipelines inspect video items: analyzeBlackFrames runs
       blackdetect=d=1.2:pix_th=0.07:pic_th=0.995 to extract black-screen intervals and total duration
       for      break    detection      or       scheduling,   while   analyzeAudioLevel          runs     two-pass/JSON
       loudnorm=I=-16:TP=-1.5:LRA=11 measurement to calculate input LUFS, true peak, and recommended
       normalization gain (clamped to -12 dB..+12 dB). Results are saved to network.json and pushed to the
       renderer via IPC events.

       4. TheTVDB v4 Metadata Lookup & SafeStorage

       [0011] After Hours TV authenticates against the TheTVDB v4 API (https://api4.thetvdb.com/v4/
       login) using a saved API key and optional subscriber PIN stored encrypted via Electron's safeStorage in
       tvdb-credentials.bin. Title normalization, folder-series inference, token/edit-distance similarity scoring,
       and editorial/promo filtering match items to episodes, series, or movies, recording metadata fields, genres, release
       years, and English programming eligibility.

       5. RetroCast View & LAN Phone Companion Remote

       [0012] A dedicated WebContentsView loads https://weather.com/retro/, injects retro contrast/
       saturation styling plus scanline and vignette overlays, dynamically positions or hides bounds on demand, and
       manages audio muting/volume and site sound-toggle activation. Geolocation permission checks and requests are
       restricted to the main file-origin view and weather.com / *.weather.com origins.

       [0013] An HTTP server on port 8765 serves renderer/mobile-remote.html at / and /remote,
       provides /api/info and rate-limited 6-digit PIN pairing at /api/pair to issue session bearer tokens, reads
       window.tvStatus at /api/status, and dispatches remote commands (channel-up, channel-down,
       play-pause, mute, volume-up, volume-down, tune) alongside PipeWire/wpctl system volume
       control.




