   BACKGROUND OF THE INVENTION AND PRIOR ART

   [0003] Conventional poison control and public safety triage systems depend heavily on fragmented,
   unstructured Safety Data Sheet (SDS) PDF documents. When handling acute exposure incidents,
   specialists are forced to perform manual text searches through thousands of static files, leading to severe
   cognitive load, delayed decision-making, and high risks of human error during critical life-safety windows.

   [0004] Furthermore, existing solutions lack dynamic multi-variable chemical interaction processing.
   When callers expose themselves to multiple compounds, legacy platforms fail to resolve complex n-ary
   reaction matrices in real-time. Moreover, existing emergency medical service (EMS) mobile data terminals
   require paramedics to read dense textual reports on bouncing displays while en route, creating unnecessary
   operational friction and delaying pre-arrival equipment preparation.

   [0005] Accordingly, there is a critical need for an integrated system that decouples complex toxicology
   logic from natural language user inputs, delivers rapid step-by-step triage index cards with direct deep-
   linked PDF proof anchors, supports mid-call dynamic re-indexing, and synthesizes hands-free en-route
   audio instructions for responding emergency personnel.




