   DETAILED DESCRIPTION OF PREFERRED EMBODIMENTS

   [0010] Referring to FIGS. 1-3, the system comprises four core operational subsystems: (1) The Pre-Flight
   Intake and Relational Combinatorics Engine, (2) The Dual-Layer Index Card and Source PDF Archiver, (3)
   The Dynamic Mid-Call Delta Re-Indexing Module, and (4) The EMS Pre-Arrival Audio Staging Network.

   1. PRE-FLIGHT INTAKE AND RELATIONAL COMBINATORICS ENGINE

   [0011] The operator interface implements a structured pre-flight checklist capturing subject biometrics
   (age, weight, gender), exposure timeline, and ingested or contacted substances. Natural language inputs
   automatically map to standardized CAS/UN chemical identifiers using alias lookup tables.

   [0012] For compound mixtures (e.g., bleach, acid, and alkaline buffers), the system evaluates an n-ary
   chemical interaction matrix $M_{chem}$. The net toxicity score $T_{net}$ for compounds $C = \{c_1,
   c_2, \dots, c_n\}$ given biometric factors $B$ is computed as:


      T_{net}(C, B) = \phi(B) \cdot \left[ \sum_{i=1}^{n} Severity(c_i) +
      \sum_{i=1}^{n} \sum_{j > i}^{n} Interaction(c_i, c_j) \right]


   [0013] Bounded variable logic evaluates worst-case chemical categories when proprietary trade-secret
   formulas are encountered, guaranteeing immediate triage safety advice without requiring specific
   manufacturer ingredient breakdowns.



