   2. DUAL-LAYER INDEX CARD AND SOURCE PDF ARCHIVER

   [0014] Upon intake processing, the system generates a dual-layer output. The top layer displays a high-
   contrast emergency index card restricted to 3-5 prioritized, actionable instructions (e.g., evacuation, oral
   flushing, contraindication warnings).

   [0015] The underlying compliance layer maintains active index pointers to local PDF safety repositories.
   The system generates direct deep-links $L_{anchor}$ to the source document page and bounding box
   coordinates $(x, y, w, h)$ containing relevant chemical warnings:

      L_{anchor}(c_i) = URI(PDF_{c_i}) \mathbin{\Vert} PageNum
      \mathbin{\Vert} BoundingBox(x, y, w, h)


   [0016] This dual-layer structure guarantees instantaneous operational response for first responders while
   maintaining audit-ready regulatory and legal verification.

   3. DYNAMIC MID-CALL DELTA RE-INDEXING MODULE

   [0017] To accommodate mid-call disclosures (e.g., newly remembered secondary substances or emerging
   symptoms), the operator UI provides dedicated dynamic update fields below the primary index card while
   locking static biometric parameters.

   [0018] Entering a secondary compound triggers an instantaneous differential search. The system updates
   the triage card and computes a differential telemetry delta vector $\Delta P$, transmitting only changed
   parameters across the offline sub-GHz packet network to minimize bandwidth consumption during critical
   events.

   4. EMS PRE-ARRIVAL AUDIO STAGING NETWORK

   [0019] Responding emergency medical vehicles receive the structured telemetry packet and extract a
   prioritized "EMS Staging Briefing." An offline, local neural text-to-speech (TTS) engine synthesizes and
   broadcasts the briefing over the vehicle cabin audio system.

   [0020] The audio loop automatically announces patient metrics, primary hazards, suggested equipment
   staging (e.g., high-flow oxygen, specific antidote kits, airway tools), and contraindications, enabling
   paramedics to prepare medical gear hands-free while en route.


